;. /plan_continuation_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition plan_continuation
  ;= Propose a continuation for the same work
    This flow returns native values. Use the retain_result writer for a standalone occurrence. Compose project_result when a Nenex document is wanted. Publish the named child flows before publishing this composition; their exact definitions are captured.

    ;@ /flow/input assessment
    ;= assessment

    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= sources

    ;@ /flow/input provider
    ;= provider

    ;@ /flow/step task ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/stages/continuation
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;@ /flow/bind context assessment
    ;= task

    ;@ /flow/step answered ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/interactive_requests
    ;@ /flow/bind tasks task
    ;@ /flow/bind provider provider
    ;= answered

    ;@ /flow/step result ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/stages/results
    ;@ /flow/bind responses answered
    ;= result

    ;@ /flow/result result
    ;= Propose a continuation for the same work result

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;= Propose a continuation for the same work
      Read the native assessment and explicitly bound task evidence. Return reason, required_input, next_action and note. Preserve the original work owner and identity. Explain what input or permission is missing and which declared action could continue that work. Running work should be observed, completed work should be checked, and paused work requires an explicit resume decision. Do not invoke any action, change status, adopt another definition or start replacement work. Use "None required" only when the evidence establishes it. This is a proposal, not a completed continuation.
